AB  - The existing difficulties of programming education are individualized guidance resources are lacking, and there is insufficient time for teachers to provide feedback, and the student’s basic knowledge is very different. To support people in the programming course, this paper presents a programming course support system using Generative Artificial Intelligence (GAI). It is based on a Large Language Model (LLM) as the core engine of the system to realize intelligent tutoring, which includes three phases: Knowledge base construction, Prompt engineering optimization, and Multi-turn dialogue mechanism design. An organized Knowledge base is first created that consists of knowledge points concerning the courses, examples of code and frequent mistakes. Secondly, prompt templates are created with role positioning, task constrains, and output format specifications. Finally, a multi-turn interaction mechanism is presented which involves the interaction context. The system is being used in a university with 120 students as its pilots. Compared to the control group, code debugging time is reduced by 37.6%, and homework scores steadily increased from 74.1 to 91.8, with a satisfaction rate of 90% (4.3 points). This technical solution provides a feasible path for the intelligentization of programming education, effectively alleviating teacher workload and improving teaching quality.
