AB  - Increasing competition in software development is accelerating the pace of delivery. At the same time, it remains crucial to maintain software quality and prevent budget overruns. One potential solution to the issues of low quality and excessive costs is the use of transformer-based large language models (LLMs). In recent years, an increasing number of development teams have sought to adopt artificial intelligence for code generation, with the intention of partially or potentially fully replacing junior-level development tasks. This study includes a comprehensive literature review and extensive testing of different prompt engineering approaches for LLMs. The results identify which software development tasks can be effectively delegated to transformer-based models, how to formulate prompts to achieve the desired outcomes, and what level of task decomposition ensures acceptable code quality.
