AB  - The rapid advancement of large language models (LLMs) has offered an excellent view and outlook in automated software engineering. The present article presents a novel Multi agent, LLM powered system named AI Code Factory, which en codes the plain English prompts into full-stack web applications that are able to be deployed using formal Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC). The system executes and finishes five AI-aided design phases Project Overview, Requirements engineering, User Research, Task flow analysis and User stories before proceed ing to a stepwise automated code generation path Strategist, Architect, Coder, Test, and Self-Repair agents organized by LangGraph. It also has a React-based interactive IDE which supports streamlining real-time, retention of projects in SQLite, version history which is rollback-capable, and multi-provider support of LLM such as Groq Llama-3.3-70B and Google Gemini with automatic rate-limit backups. An experimental trial of 20 sample application prompts shows that the system creates high-quality syntactically sound and deployable React and Flask applications where over 91% of the self-portemization attempts are successful after re-engineering. The architecture introduces innovative concepts of stage-gated SDLC execution, displayed interactive drawings and unified project management that are considered to be some worthwhile additions to the growing art of software synthesis through LLM.
ER  - 

